WEBVTT

00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:11.580
Mr. Kureko! Um...

00:00:11.580 --> 00:00:16.160
If you're free... Would you like to go get some
food sometime tomorrow or the day after?

00:00:16.160 --> 00:00:20.000
I've got a deadline for a script
coming up this week...

00:00:20.870 --> 00:00:22.660
Okay...

00:00:22.660 --> 00:00:23.580
Good night.

00:00:23.580 --> 00:00:25.910
Are you really quitting?

00:00:29.790 --> 00:00:33.580
Technically, my contract ends next March.

00:00:33.580 --> 00:00:36.250
Oh... I see.

00:00:36.250 --> 00:00:40.660
The Ranzo Arakawa Prize... I hope you get it.

00:00:40.660 --> 00:00:43.870
I'm way past the age to receive
a newcomer's award.

00:00:47.660 --> 00:00:51.250
But for a writer who hasn't been able
to get on in the world for 52 years,

00:00:51.250 --> 00:00:55.580
if there were any turning points
in life left for me, this would be it.

00:00:55.580 --> 00:00:58.250
I'm surprised myself.

00:00:58.250 --> 00:01:03.040
That I still have the desire to change at all...

00:02:47.160 --> 00:02:47.910
"Episode 10: I Have to Do This"

00:02:47.910 --> 00:02:50.330
"Episode 10: I Have to Do This"
You look as if a curse was lifted off of you.

00:02:50.330 --> 00:02:52.120
Really?

00:02:52.120 --> 00:02:56.370
To me she looks as if she fell into
the darkness and can't get out of it.

00:02:56.370 --> 00:02:59.500
So Minare, give us an idea of how it went.

00:02:59.500 --> 00:03:02.200
This is my fifth cup of coffee today...

00:03:02.200 --> 00:03:04.000
Well...

00:03:04.000 --> 00:03:06.660
If I were to sum up what happened today...

00:03:06.660 --> 00:03:08.000
I'd say it went like this.

00:03:08.000 --> 00:03:09.910
Huh? Hm...

00:03:09.910 --> 00:03:10.830
I don't understand.

00:03:10.830 --> 00:03:15.370
We climbed Mt. Moiwa... He bought me
a trinket... No one's done that in a while.

00:03:15.370 --> 00:03:19.370
We went to a movie then rode
a Ferris wheel... Oh, it was a blast.

00:03:19.370 --> 00:03:22.000
You're telling me you just
went on a boring old date?

00:03:24.910 --> 00:03:27.620
Mizuho, you understand
the cuteness of this, right?

00:03:27.620 --> 00:03:29.410
Yes, I sure do.

00:03:29.410 --> 00:03:31.540
You're further away from
getting a smartphone now.

00:03:31.540 --> 00:03:33.080
Wait a minute!

00:03:33.080 --> 00:03:35.910
Maybe... That thing in the trash can...

00:03:35.910 --> 00:03:39.410
Now that I think about it, maybe he
tried to cook for himself and failed,

00:03:39.410 --> 00:03:42.450
and he was just being self-deprecating
in order to avoid the issue.

00:03:42.450 --> 00:03:46.000
Or maybe that neighbor upstairs related to the
oil executive is a gay guy who likes to cook,

00:03:46.000 --> 00:03:48.450
and was like, "Hey, what did you
eat yesterday?" Ah!

00:03:48.450 --> 00:03:51.080
If that's true, then I've made a huge mistake!

00:03:51.080 --> 00:03:56.500
Well, I'll listen to the details
over a drink another day.

00:03:56.500 --> 00:03:59.200
Do you have it right now?

00:03:59.200 --> 00:04:02.330
I'm honestly regretting this right now,

00:04:02.330 --> 00:04:05.160
but I'm the one who suggested
the idea in the first place.

00:04:05.160 --> 00:04:07.620
Besides his name, there's no mention
of personal information,

00:04:07.620 --> 00:04:11.160
and we didn't have sex,
so feel free to use any part of it.

00:04:11.160 --> 00:04:12.620
All right, all right.

00:04:12.620 --> 00:04:15.250
It's fine if you did though.

00:04:15.250 --> 00:04:18.290
Kakoton, Kakoen, there's a job for you.

00:04:18.290 --> 00:04:20.660
Come to the control room in 20 minutes.

00:04:20.660 --> 00:04:21.790
Who was that?

00:04:21.790 --> 00:04:24.000
Once known as the "great generals of sound,"

00:04:24.000 --> 00:04:27.250
they're the sound effects masters
who suffer great misfortune in radio.

00:04:27.250 --> 00:04:29.580
"Sound effects"
The job of sound effects technicians,
or sound engineers,

00:04:29.580 --> 00:04:31.620
"Sound effects"
is to create many different types of sounds.

00:04:31.620 --> 00:04:32.500
"Sound effects"
Cool.

00:04:32.500 --> 00:04:34.450
The legendary duo has finally been summoned!

00:04:34.450 --> 00:04:35.370
Legendary?

00:04:35.370 --> 00:04:36.750
Nobody knows their real names.

00:04:36.750 --> 00:04:38.500
What kind of company is this?!

00:04:38.500 --> 00:04:42.830
Minare, the next broadcast
of Wave, Listen to Me!

00:04:42.830 --> 00:04:45.120
is on Saturday at 3:30 AM.

00:04:45.120 --> 00:04:47.370
During that broadcast...

00:04:49.250 --> 00:04:51.580
You're going to bury Mitsuo.

00:04:54.200 --> 00:04:56.120
What? You're moving out?

00:04:56.120 --> 00:05:00.290
Sorry to bring this up when you're having
feelings about Mr. Kureko quitting...

00:05:00.290 --> 00:05:02.620
But I can't keep on letting you spoil me.

00:05:02.620 --> 00:05:04.700
I wouldn't mind if you stayed forever.

00:05:04.700 --> 00:05:08.160
Still, I can't do that to you...

00:05:08.160 --> 00:05:09.620
And despite what I just said,

00:05:09.620 --> 00:05:13.500
I still would appreciate if you let me
stay here for a few more days.

00:05:13.500 --> 00:05:15.200
But why so suddenly?

00:05:15.200 --> 00:05:18.660
You know... I realized this after
the whole ordeal the other day...

00:05:18.660 --> 00:05:23.330
You only deteriorate as a person if you
get used to relying on others' kindness.

00:05:23.330 --> 00:05:29.000
But you've been a great help feeding
the turtles for me while I'm at work.

00:05:29.000 --> 00:05:31.080
You guys don't want her to go either, right?

00:05:31.080 --> 00:05:32.620
--Food?
--It's food!

00:05:32.620 --> 00:05:34.290
--See? They're saying they'll miss you!
--Oh? It's horse mackerel flakes!

00:05:34.290 --> 00:05:38.040
I appreciate the act, Mizuho. I'm tearing up.

00:05:43.580 --> 00:05:45.000
Oh! By any chance...

00:05:45.000 --> 00:05:45.830
Huh? What?

00:05:45.830 --> 00:05:48.750
Are you going to be living with Mr. Mitsuo now?

00:05:48.750 --> 00:05:50.620
Of course not!

00:05:50.620 --> 00:05:54.450
But you guys were together
up until just a few months ago, right?

00:05:54.450 --> 00:05:58.330
Didn't it make you think of all sorts
of things? Seeing him again?

00:05:58.330 --> 00:06:03.250
Well... To be honest, this is what I realized

00:06:03.250 --> 00:06:08.700
that I tend to fall for guys like Mitsuo...

00:06:08.700 --> 00:06:15.580
As you can see... when I'm single,
I can live carelessly day-by-day...

00:06:15.580 --> 00:06:18.910
But when I have a boyfriend,
I really devote myself to him.

00:06:18.910 --> 00:06:21.540
I really want to take care of him.

00:06:21.540 --> 00:06:27.120
I worry if he's hungry or if he's
cold while he's sleeping.

00:06:27.120 --> 00:06:28.700
Funny, I know.

00:06:28.700 --> 00:06:33.870
Well, it's true that he turned out
to be more of a slob than I am.

00:06:33.870 --> 00:06:38.410
But that's why when he would tell me things like
"Delicious," "It's so warm," or "Thank you,"

00:06:38.410 --> 00:06:41.160
all with a smile on his face--
it made me so happy.

00:06:41.160 --> 00:06:46.410
I feel a sense of pleasure
knowing that I'm spoiling him.

00:06:46.410 --> 00:06:50.450
But don't men who can do everything
on their own make you worry?

00:06:50.450 --> 00:06:55.870
It makes me wonder if I'm needed
in that person's life.

00:06:55.870 --> 00:06:57.410
Morning.

00:06:57.410 --> 00:07:00.950
Miss Minare, could you try this for us?

00:07:00.950 --> 00:07:04.040
Isn't that boiled squid?
Did you change the seasoning?

00:07:04.040 --> 00:07:05.500
It sure looks like it, right?

00:07:05.500 --> 00:07:07.290
Oh...

00:07:07.290 --> 00:07:09.160
Hm? Is this wheat gluten?

00:07:09.160 --> 00:07:13.410
Yes, I wanted to develop
a vegetarian seafood curry!

00:07:13.410 --> 00:07:17.080
"Strong thirst for knowledge!"
"Completely missing the point!!"
There's a fine line between having
a strong thirst for knowledge

00:07:17.080 --> 00:07:18.830
"Strong thirst for knowledge!"
"Completely missing the point!!"
and completely missing the point.

00:07:18.830 --> 00:07:22.040
Will you do the honors and
name this dish, Miss Minare?

00:07:22.040 --> 00:07:24.000
Huh?! Why me?!

00:07:24.000 --> 00:07:28.790
When I mentioned how I thought
you seemed unfriendly recently,

00:07:28.790 --> 00:07:35.000
Miss Tachibana brought up how you might be
annoyed with all the new additions on the menu.

00:07:35.000 --> 00:07:37.200
And it all made sense.

00:07:37.200 --> 00:07:39.040
Oh... Well, I appreciate the thought.

00:07:39.040 --> 00:07:41.080
I'm feeling some love in the air.

00:07:41.080 --> 00:07:43.910
So, what do you think about that, Miss Minare?

00:07:46.040 --> 00:07:48.790
Oh, the texture's similar plus it's tasty.

00:07:48.790 --> 00:07:52.040
Everything you've made has been great so far.

00:07:52.040 --> 00:07:53.120
Unlike Manager.

00:07:53.120 --> 00:07:54.500
You really mean it?!

00:07:54.500 --> 00:07:59.040
I probably don't even need to ask,
but you cook for yourself at home, right?

00:07:59.040 --> 00:08:02.950
What? Oh, that's right.
Unless I go out with my friends.

00:08:02.950 --> 00:08:04.830
Do you clean your place every week?

00:08:04.830 --> 00:08:07.250
Well, yeah, more like three times a week.

00:08:07.250 --> 00:08:08.910
Do you also know how to sew?

00:08:08.910 --> 00:08:11.040
I've been getting into leather crafts recently,

00:08:11.040 --> 00:08:13.750
and I finally mastered how to sew
on a miter joint.

00:08:13.750 --> 00:08:15.370
Agh... You're no good.

00:08:15.370 --> 00:08:19.330
Wait a minute! Why would any of that
make you disappointed?

00:08:22.700 --> 00:08:24.410
Hello?

00:08:24.410 --> 00:08:26.790
Oh... Hey...

00:08:26.790 --> 00:08:29.080
Huh? Oh, I don't know.

00:08:29.080 --> 00:08:32.450
At about eight hours and 52 minutes?
That doesn't really help...

00:08:32.450 --> 00:08:34.540
What are we talking about?

00:08:35.500 --> 00:08:38.790
Oh, sorry. I can't hear clearly
when you try to imitate our voices.

00:08:38.790 --> 00:08:40.540
Oh, that's when we got on the Ferris wheel.

00:08:40.540 --> 00:08:43.200
Can't you tell by the Miku Hatsune
song playing in the background?

00:08:43.200 --> 00:08:46.040
You never been on it before? Well, okay.

00:08:46.040 --> 00:08:48.580
--Huh? Oh, that's the sound of me crushing him
when he was about to kiss me.

00:08:48.580 --> 00:08:50.870
--What?!
--Huh? Oh, that's the sound of me crushing him
when he was about to kiss me.

00:08:50.870 --> 00:08:54.580
No, of course not. I just warned him
not to push his luck.

00:08:54.580 --> 00:08:56.580
Huh? Oh...

00:08:56.580 --> 00:08:59.410
I was sitting next to him.

00:08:59.410 --> 00:09:01.750
Well, yeah, I know...

00:09:01.750 --> 00:09:04.450
It was easy as easy gets...

00:09:04.450 --> 00:09:08.200
It was more a self-respect
kinda thing. How's that?

00:09:08.200 --> 00:09:11.200
Oh, okay. Yeah, it's all fine.

00:09:11.200 --> 00:09:14.200
You're probably not giving me
the script until the last minute, anyway.

00:09:14.200 --> 00:09:17.000
Got it, got it. Improvisation...

00:09:17.000 --> 00:09:21.500
It's all about the improvisations, right?
What a jazzy radio station.

00:09:21.500 --> 00:09:24.500
This really isn't funny, you know?

00:09:24.500 --> 00:09:26.750
Yeah. Okay.

00:09:26.750 --> 00:09:30.370
I'll see you tonight. All right. Bye.

00:09:31.160 --> 00:09:32.040
Huh?

00:09:32.040 --> 00:09:34.910
Stare...

00:09:34.910 --> 00:09:37.910
Oh, right. I met up with Mitsuo the other day.

00:09:39.410 --> 00:09:40.250
What--?!

00:09:40.250 --> 00:09:42.750
Oh, well nothing major happened.

00:09:42.750 --> 00:09:45.700
We climbed a mountain, drank,
went for a movie, gazed at the view...

00:09:45.700 --> 00:09:48.160
Then we went to Mitsuo's to drink again...

00:09:49.540 --> 00:09:51.910
Then I poked into his hole, that's all.

00:09:55.450 --> 00:09:57.370
Um, excuse me.

00:09:57.370 --> 00:09:59.080
Yes, I'll be right there.

00:09:59.080 --> 00:10:01.330
I thought we ordered the lamb...

00:10:01.330 --> 00:10:03.200
Oh, I'm terribly sorry.

00:10:03.200 --> 00:10:05.080
My husband's Indian, so...

00:10:05.080 --> 00:10:06.540
Excuse me, miss.

00:10:06.540 --> 00:10:08.080
Yes, I'll be right there.

00:10:08.080 --> 00:10:11.660
We're getting complaints left and right!
Get a hold of yourself, Acting Manager!

00:10:11.660 --> 00:10:14.410
Don't let your emotions get the better of you.
Show your pride as a professional!

00:10:14.410 --> 00:10:18.500
Sorry. I know it must be frustrating
to hear that from me.

00:10:18.500 --> 00:10:20.000
Huh...?

00:10:20.000 --> 00:10:23.160
I apologize... I'll do my best...

00:10:23.160 --> 00:10:24.040
Uh...

00:10:24.040 --> 00:10:25.910
Miss Koda, may I have a word?

00:10:25.910 --> 00:10:27.950
I sense a silent anger...

00:10:30.500 --> 00:10:33.750
You are aware of Mr. Nakahara's
feelings, aren't you?

00:10:33.750 --> 00:10:35.290
Oh... Yeah...

00:10:35.290 --> 00:10:37.330
He was listening in on my phone conversation,

00:10:37.330 --> 00:10:40.000
so I didn't think it was necessary
to keep it a secret.

00:10:40.000 --> 00:10:41.620
Miss Koda.

00:10:41.620 --> 00:10:44.620
Will you please stop making
a fool out of Mr. Nakahara?

00:10:44.620 --> 00:10:45.620
Huh?!

00:10:45.620 --> 00:10:48.790
Why the heck do you have to tell me that?

00:10:48.790 --> 00:10:54.120
Yes... I know he may dye his hair
only in the center of his head...

00:10:54.120 --> 00:10:58.580
But he's very kind and
actually extremely sensitive.

00:10:58.580 --> 00:11:02.950
You don't have to tell me.
I've known him longer than you.

00:11:02.950 --> 00:11:04.250
Miss Koda...

00:11:04.250 --> 00:11:07.540
I'm very happy to hear
that you got back together

00:11:07.540 --> 00:11:10.120
with the man you said you wanted to kill.

00:11:10.120 --> 00:11:13.080
Well don't be because I didn't
get back together with him!

00:11:13.080 --> 00:11:17.910
Then please just stop toying with Mr. Nakahara.

00:11:17.910 --> 00:11:19.410
Will you...?

00:11:20.370 --> 00:11:24.830
Just now, too. You didn't
have to say any of that.

00:11:24.830 --> 00:11:28.120
Oh, come on! And what do you mean
"stop toying with him"?

00:11:28.120 --> 00:11:32.250
That's all I have to say.
I apologize for my impertinence.

00:11:32.250 --> 00:11:34.160
I'm going back to work.

00:11:34.160 --> 00:11:38.790
If you're that worried,
then why don't you comfort him?

00:11:38.790 --> 00:11:41.120
You guys are living together, after all.

00:11:43.000 --> 00:11:47.410
He's letting me stay at his place,
but we're not living together.

00:11:47.410 --> 00:11:51.870
And it's... very frustrating.

00:11:55.120 --> 00:11:59.200
What's the difference? Ugh, that woman
gets on my nerves! And me, too!

00:11:59.200 --> 00:12:01.080
And what?! Stop making a fool out of him?!

00:12:01.080 --> 00:12:03.620
Nakahara would be happy to hear it!

00:12:03.620 --> 00:12:07.410
I retrieved half of the money I lent
and gave him physical damage!

00:12:07.410 --> 00:12:09.620
It's possible he may even be dead.

00:12:09.620 --> 00:12:11.500
That's all he needs to hear!

00:12:11.500 --> 00:12:13.830
Are you venting out all your
private life's worries?

00:12:13.830 --> 00:12:16.450
Yeah, but I still have more to let out.

00:12:16.450 --> 00:12:17.870
Come on.

00:12:17.870 --> 00:12:19.910
There's a special guest waiting on you.

00:12:23.660 --> 00:12:25.910
There are lots of beads on this.

00:12:25.910 --> 00:12:28.160
What is this fan used for?

00:12:28.160 --> 00:12:30.410
That's used to create rain.

00:12:30.410 --> 00:12:32.790
Try holding it like this and shaking it.

00:12:33.700 --> 00:12:35.080
Wow.

00:12:35.080 --> 00:12:38.950
It's the sound of rain falling on the roof.

00:12:38.950 --> 00:12:41.500
When you shake another one like this,

00:12:41.500 --> 00:12:44.750
the sound becomes even more delicate.

00:12:44.750 --> 00:12:46.370
Wow...

00:12:48.950 --> 00:12:53.040
This is the whistle that can produce
all those comical sounds.

00:12:53.040 --> 00:12:55.330
By adjusting the slide,

00:12:55.330 --> 00:13:00.950
you can create anything from sounds of
baseballs flying to realistic ghost sounds.

00:13:00.950 --> 00:13:02.870
Wow, it really does sound like it.

00:13:02.870 --> 00:13:05.200
You're not gonna question
"realistic ghost sounds"?

00:13:05.200 --> 00:13:06.910
How about this paper cup?

00:13:06.910 --> 00:13:09.000
I don't know, what could it be?

00:13:09.000 --> 00:13:11.120
Try holding it up and fidgeting with the string.

00:13:12.830 --> 00:13:14.870
Ah, it's the sound of the wind.

00:13:14.870 --> 00:13:16.500
Cool, huh?

00:13:16.500 --> 00:13:19.200
Bet you didn't expect that sound
from just looking at that thing.

00:13:19.200 --> 00:13:21.330
My, it's been so long!

00:13:21.330 --> 00:13:25.950
We've been using these tools
since we started at the radio station.

00:13:25.950 --> 00:13:27.950
That was around 1965...

00:13:27.950 --> 00:13:31.580
Recording equipment wasn't
as advanced back then.

00:13:31.580 --> 00:13:35.080
That's why we tried to create
sounds like these in the studio.

00:13:35.080 --> 00:13:39.200
But gradually as technology developed,
these things became more and more obsolete.

00:13:39.200 --> 00:13:42.450
Hey, show her that thing you're best at.

00:13:42.450 --> 00:13:43.500
You mean this?

00:13:45.160 --> 00:13:47.870
Amazing! It sounds just like a horse galloping!

00:13:47.870 --> 00:13:51.120
You can produce over 200 sounds
with just your hands and mouth, right?

00:13:51.120 --> 00:13:54.830
The girls at the hostess bar
love it when I show off.

00:13:54.830 --> 00:13:57.250
The only time we really got
to go all out with our skills

00:13:57.250 --> 00:13:59.410
was when we did "The Galactic Campaign."

00:13:59.410 --> 00:14:02.160
Ah, "The Galactic Campaign"! That takes me back.

00:14:02.160 --> 00:14:03.540
That was written by Sugi, right?

00:14:03.540 --> 00:14:07.450
We created sounds to differentiate
all 500 spaceships.

00:14:07.450 --> 00:14:10.000
Stardate 4,050.

00:14:10.000 --> 00:14:12.290
To fight against the atrocity
of the ultra-galactic empire,

00:14:12.290 --> 00:14:16.330
a rebel fleet that transcends
star systems was formed.

00:14:16.330 --> 00:14:18.950
It consists of over 500 ships!

00:14:21.450 --> 00:14:25.410
Yam, yam, yam. Rowee, rowee.
Bam, bam, bam. Pshh..

00:14:25.410 --> 00:14:26.500
Peepeeeep!

00:14:26.500 --> 00:14:27.660
Lukkora, lukkora!

00:14:27.660 --> 00:14:29.660
En, en, en. Bupupup!

00:14:29.660 --> 00:14:31.200
Psh...

00:14:31.200 --> 00:14:33.750
Am I collaborating with comedians today?

00:14:33.750 --> 00:14:36.250
What makes you think we're comedians?

00:14:36.250 --> 00:14:38.500
Minare, let me introduce you.

00:14:38.500 --> 00:14:42.120
They're the legendary sound effects masters
everyone in the industry knows about.

00:14:42.120 --> 00:14:44.870
Meet Kakoton and Kakoen.

00:14:44.870 --> 00:14:49.700
When they retired at the radio station in Osaka,
I begged them to come to us.

00:14:49.700 --> 00:14:51.370
As part-time employees.

00:14:51.370 --> 00:14:54.870
No, no. You're the one who did us a favor, Mato.

00:14:54.870 --> 00:15:00.200
If we had stayed at that old joint, we would've
ended up a dried pig and a mummified monkey.

00:15:00.200 --> 00:15:02.580
But we're not in high demand around here either.

00:15:02.580 --> 00:15:06.000
When we thought we had finally
learned Cubase and SONAR,

00:15:06.000 --> 00:15:10.200
the station told us they were going
to outsource the task. Boy, what a drag.

00:15:10.200 --> 00:15:13.870
Sound effects technicians from ancient
times like us who can only work

00:15:13.870 --> 00:15:15.790
with analog equipment
are a useless pair.

00:15:15.790 --> 00:15:17.330
Get it? Like a pear?

00:15:17.410 --> 00:15:19.410
"Self-deprecation + Bad pun = Nuisance"

00:15:19.790 --> 00:15:21.540
We called them in today because--

00:15:21.540 --> 00:15:23.580
Yeah, right. I get it.

00:15:23.580 --> 00:15:26.950
This program doesn't have the funds
to outsource sound effects, right?

00:15:26.950 --> 00:15:27.870
Bzzz. Wrong.

00:15:27.870 --> 00:15:28.830
Huh?

00:15:28.830 --> 00:15:32.120
That's 85% correct.

00:15:32.120 --> 00:15:35.500
That's quite high. It's rather depressing.

00:15:35.500 --> 00:15:38.910
What costs the most when you
outsource is the jingle.

00:15:38.910 --> 00:15:42.830
As long as it's not a rare sound effect,
we can take care of it using sounds

00:15:42.830 --> 00:15:45.290
from the compilation that's been
purchased from JASRAC.

00:15:45.290 --> 00:15:47.500
We called them in because
they are the only ones

00:15:47.500 --> 00:15:53.500
who can engineer the particular sounds
we need for our next broadcast.

00:15:53.910 --> 00:15:56.700
Ah, testing, testing.

00:15:56.700 --> 00:15:59.000
Mina, can you hear me?

00:15:59.000 --> 00:16:05.200
On our date last time, you mentioned that you
didn't have the Morisu boxers, right?

00:16:05.200 --> 00:16:07.830
I actually had them! They were
in my room this whole time.

00:16:07.830 --> 00:16:12.250
You'll take them if they're free, right?
Even if they're for men?

00:16:12.250 --> 00:16:14.700
I was wondering if we could go on
another date when I give them to you.

00:16:14.700 --> 00:16:19.200
--Mr. Mato, what is this?
I don't remember him saying this.
--Yeah, we might as well go on a date if
I'm going to see you. Let's go on a date.

00:16:19.200 --> 00:16:22.910
Did you go meet with Mitsuo
without telling me and record this?

00:16:22.910 --> 00:16:26.120
How am I supposed to track him down
when I don't even know his face,

00:16:26.120 --> 00:16:29.040
full name, address,
phone number or e-mail address?

00:16:29.040 --> 00:16:30.160
What?

00:16:30.160 --> 00:16:34.750
But well, if it makes you say that
then their hard work surely paid off.

00:16:34.750 --> 00:16:36.080
--What?
--What?

00:16:37.370 --> 00:16:39.790
This fine work was made by
manipulating the sample I prepared

00:16:39.790 --> 00:16:43.660
to create something that sounds
just like Mitsuo's voice.

00:16:45.000 --> 00:16:47.200
Today's broadcast is tailored
to be a radio drama.

00:16:47.200 --> 00:16:49.450
But of course, this is all going to be live.

00:16:49.450 --> 00:16:53.330
And those moldy props brought
in by the legendary duo

00:16:53.330 --> 00:16:54.950
to entertain the young employees...

00:16:54.950 --> 00:16:56.750
Excuse you!

00:16:56.750 --> 00:17:00.080
We might as well put them to use!
It's a dead-of-night slot.

00:17:00.080 --> 00:17:04.500
Hold on, then why did you make me
record the whole date with Mitsuo?!

00:17:04.500 --> 00:17:09.540
Well, of course I'd be opposed to you
playing the whole thing unedited...

00:17:09.540 --> 00:17:12.040
The script is written by
mimicking speech patterns,

00:17:12.040 --> 00:17:14.830
so the more samples we have, the better.

00:17:14.830 --> 00:17:16.700
Sorry, miss.

00:17:16.700 --> 00:17:21.200
If we could've prepared the sound earlier,
we would've been able to record the day before.

00:17:21.200 --> 00:17:24.290
But this guy struggled with the waveform
editing so it wasn't ready until today.

00:17:24.290 --> 00:17:26.290
You're the one who threw everything onto me!

00:17:26.290 --> 00:17:29.870
You're the one who said you wanted to
try editing on that Audition software!

00:17:29.870 --> 00:17:32.950
You don't know anything!
You've never used Audition before!

00:17:32.950 --> 00:17:36.450
--So what was the task that could
only be done by these two?
--It's because you're not
well-versed with acronyms!

00:17:36.450 --> 00:17:37.870
--Who else has the time
to do all this tedious work?
--Shut up, you monkey! You fossil!

00:17:37.870 --> 00:17:39.620
--Who else has the time
to do all this tedious work?
--I'll kill you! You incompetent DAW user!

00:17:39.620 --> 00:17:40.830
--Who else has the time
to do all this tedious work?
--You're the one who's incompetent with DAWs!

00:17:40.830 --> 00:17:43.080
--Anyway... Let me ask you this before we start,
what is the radio drama about?
--You're the one who's incompetent with DAWs!

00:17:43.080 --> 00:17:46.790
--Anyway... Let me ask you this before we start,
what is the radio drama about?
--I am not!

00:17:46.790 --> 00:17:48.040
It's probably another--

00:17:48.040 --> 00:17:50.700
Like I said before...

00:17:50.700 --> 00:17:52.330
It's a burial.

00:17:54.500 --> 00:17:58.410
This isn't just Mitsuo's--
it's also your burial, too.

00:17:58.410 --> 00:17:59.790
What?

00:17:59.790 --> 00:18:03.950
You're the talkative woman who gets
tossed around by her love and hate

00:18:03.950 --> 00:18:05.950
for the man who betrayed her.

00:18:05.950 --> 00:18:08.910
No, it's written from your perspective
after you met me at the bar.

00:18:08.910 --> 00:18:09.750
What?

00:18:09.750 --> 00:18:12.910
It's about time we graduated from that already.

00:18:12.910 --> 00:18:16.620
You now host a program
with your name in the title

00:18:16.620 --> 00:18:21.080
and your name is printed as a DJ on the radio
and television section in the paper.

00:18:21.080 --> 00:18:24.790
Let's make you a radio personality
both in name and in reality.

00:18:24.790 --> 00:18:31.750
Tonight, along with Mitsuo,
die and reincarnate... Minare...

00:18:41.660 --> 00:18:45.200
It's been 40 years
since I've done a live radio drama!

00:18:49.250 --> 00:18:50.830
It's so heavy.

00:18:58.200 --> 00:18:59.290
Hey.

00:18:59.290 --> 00:19:01.540
Why don't you help out a little?

00:19:05.250 --> 00:19:07.580
I'm paying you to clean everything up.

00:19:07.580 --> 00:19:09.540
Let's crank up the reverb...

00:19:09.540 --> 00:19:13.410
Hey, you better think about this more seriously.

00:19:13.410 --> 00:19:17.540
The only advantage of burying a dead body in
the pouring rain is that nobody will hear us.

00:19:17.540 --> 00:19:19.500
That's about it.

00:19:19.500 --> 00:19:21.870
But otherwise, the dirt sucks up
the water and gets heavier,

00:19:21.870 --> 00:19:24.040
and even if I bury the body in the mud,

00:19:24.040 --> 00:19:27.660
there's no way to know how
it will look once it dries up.

00:19:27.660 --> 00:19:30.200
I was against doing this today.

00:19:30.200 --> 00:19:31.950
So you can't hold me accountable.

00:19:38.500 --> 00:19:43.370
I don't know why I'm even asking this now,
but why did this guy end up dead?

00:19:43.370 --> 00:19:45.290
It's none of your business.

00:19:45.290 --> 00:19:48.620
It's just small talk. I could
care less about it, really.

00:19:52.870 --> 00:19:56.580
He ran away with the money I entrusted to him.

00:19:56.580 --> 00:19:57.500
How much?

00:19:57.500 --> 00:19:58.870
Five hundred thousand yen.

00:19:58.870 --> 00:20:03.160
Are you kidding me? That's cheaper than my fee.

00:20:03.910 --> 00:20:05.200
I know, right?

00:20:05.200 --> 00:20:10.910
But for me, 500,000 yen is enough
of a reason to kill someone.

00:20:10.910 --> 00:20:14.330
The fact that he betrayed me is enough.

00:20:19.870 --> 00:20:22.790
It look longer than expected.

00:20:22.790 --> 00:20:25.370
Let's leave before the sun comes up.

00:20:26.450 --> 00:20:27.500
What is it?

00:20:41.000 --> 00:20:42.330
This is so long. Why would she kiss him
in this scenario? Is she a sex maniac?!

00:20:42.330 --> 00:20:45.330
"(50 seconds) Breathing heavily and passionately
as if it's a Latin romance."
This is so long. Why would she kiss him
in this scenario? Is she a sex maniac?!

00:20:52.660 --> 00:20:55.370
Could you give me a 100,000-yen
discount for that?

00:20:55.370 --> 00:20:59.330
You think a husband-murderer's kiss
is worth that much?

00:20:59.330 --> 00:21:01.000
That's probably more like 1,000 yen.

00:21:01.000 --> 00:21:02.540
Let's do it here before we go.

00:21:02.540 --> 00:21:04.250
No way.

00:21:04.250 --> 00:21:08.950
But we have time to stop by a hotel
before we head back to the hideout.

00:21:08.950 --> 00:21:11.540
Then let's finish this up and go.

00:21:11.540 --> 00:21:14.000
My body gets hot after I kill.

00:21:14.000 --> 00:21:16.500
What a lunatic.

00:21:16.500 --> 00:21:18.040
All right, fine.

00:21:19.700 --> 00:21:21.580
It's raining so hard.

00:21:21.580 --> 00:21:24.410
Hey, you're going to come back
and check on things later, right?

00:21:24.410 --> 00:21:26.200
Don't you need some kind of marker--?

00:21:37.950 --> 00:21:41.080
Jeez, stop that... Now's not the time...

00:21:53.660 --> 00:21:57.160
I'm getting hungry...

00:23:28.950 --> 00:23:29.950
"Next Episode"

00:23:29.950 --> 00:23:30.910
"Next Episode"
Mina...

00:23:30.910 --> 00:23:32.080
"Preview"
Mitsuo!

00:23:32.080 --> 00:23:34.620
--Let's have the master pray for us.
--What?!

00:23:34.620 --> 00:23:37.370
Cough up the karma of this life.

00:23:37.370 --> 00:23:41.200
I shall cleanse that karma
and guide your soul to a new vessel.

00:23:41.200 --> 00:23:43.330
I never asked you to cleanse me!

00:23:43.330 --> 00:23:46.750
I'm not regretting the fact
that I'm full of regret!

00:23:46.750 --> 00:23:47.910
I just want to redeem myself!

00:23:47.910 --> 00:23:49.160
Your soul will reincarnate as the chicken

00:23:49.160 --> 00:23:52.540
that'll be sold fried at the
Hot Chef section in Secoma.

00:23:52.540 --> 00:23:54.660
Hey! Were you even listening to me?!

00:23:54.660 --> 00:23:58.500
Next, on <i>Wave, Listen to Me!</i>:
"I Don't Fear Anaerobic Creatures."

00:23:58.950 --> 00:24:01.910
"See you next time!"
"Illustrated by Hiroaki Samura"
